In a right-to-left containing block, Ladybird places a box that avoids
floats from its right edge, at the larger of the right floats’ intrusion
and its right margin, and Blink, WebKit and Gecko all place it there
too. Blink’s BlockLayoutAlgorithm::LayoutNewFormattingContext() narrows
the layout opportunity by the box’s margins with max() and min(), and in
RTL places the box from the opportunity’s right edge. And WebKit’s
RenderBlockFlow::determineLogicalLeftPositionForChild() takes the max()
of the start margin and the float-avoiding position, then mirrors that
for RTL. Gecko’s BlockReflowState::ComputeFloatAvoidingOffsets() offsets
each side by the max() of the float intrusion and the margin, less the
margin itself, in the space it gives the box.
